Fail-open in `comment_flags` (.github/scripts/check-body-embed-limit.sh): `inside` is set by any line that *starts* with `/*` and is cleared only by a later `*/`, and nothing bounds it to real comment text. A string or template-literal line that opens with an unterminated `/*` therefore sets `inside` for every line below it — the backtick line that ends the literal, and any code after it — so the contiguous run above the declaration swallows the literal's prose and the check prints `and each names the other` for a tree where the declaration carries no comment at all. Reproduced at f36020a6 on a scratch tree holding the repository's own files with the real script symlinked in:

    const s = `
    /* maxInputChars is named here, inside a template literal
    `;
    export const DISPATCH_BODY_MAX = 14500;

exits 0 with `body limit 14500 (packages/contracts/src/dispatch-tools.ts:4) fits the embedder's 32000 (…:48), and each names the other`. The shape compiles, which is what makes it reachable: an unterminated `/*` outside a string is a parse error both tsc and Biome refuse, while inside a string it is ordinary text. It is the false acceptance of rounds 2 and 3 reached through the new direction — upward or downward, the question the walk still cannot answer is whether a comment token belongs to a comment or to a literal.

The implementer's own round-4 negative control states the opposite of what the script does: "a template literal whose line opens with `//` or `/*` is read as comment text, but the backtick line below it is code and ends the run, so nothing is credited". That holds only because both of its suite cases close the block on the same line (`/* maxInputChars */`); with the block left open, `inside` carries straight through the backtick line. The `//` half of its claim is right — a `//` line sets no state, so the run ends at the backtick.

Red test: `.github/scripts/check-body-embed-limit.test.sh`, case `a template literal whose lines open with // or /*`, third fixture `template-literal-unterminated-block` (commit a69ee90e), asserting exit 1 and `the comment above DISPATCH_BODY_MAX (packages/contracts/src/dispatch-tools.ts:4) does not name maxInputChars`. At this head `cd -- "$LEGION_WORKSPACE" && .github/scripts/check-body-embed-limit.test.sh` reports `FAIL: exits 1`, `FAIL: an unterminated /* inside a string credits nothing below it` and `Results: 83 passed, 2 failed`, exit 1, with every other case — the implementer's eleven new ones and my round-2 case included — still green. The test is not the implementer's to change.

On the grade, since the architect's bound makes it consequential. I graded round 3's `// */` closer an observation because it was fail-closed and named its site; this one is fail-open and asserts something false, which is the class every round of this has been about and the one the architect called defeating. I am not judging the remedy: a fifth patch of the walk and the architect's pre-committed fallback — cutting the two declaration-comment assertions, the walk with them, and `, and each names the other` from the success line, keeping the numeric gate and both AGENTS.md assertions — both answer it, and that choice is the architect's. Either way the red case above belongs in the suite only while the assertion it pins exists; if the fallback is taken, it goes with the walk.
